# 2. FILE UPLOAD MODULE

Create an attractive file upload section on the home dashboard.

The application must have exactly THREE main Excel upload sections.

### FILE 1: COMBINED SKU MASTER + BOM MASTER

The SKU Master and BOM Master are maintained in ONE Excel file.

The actual BOM format contains these six columns:

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| SKU | Finished goods SKU code |
| SKU name | Finished goods description |
| RM | Raw material / packaging material code |
| RM dec | Raw material / packaging material description |
| Uom | Unit of measurement |
| Norms | Consumption norm |

Example:

| SKU | SKU name | RM | RM dec | Uom | Norms |
|---|---|---|---|---|---:|
| 7.A.001607 | RAJNI GOLD REFINED PALMOLEIN OIL BOX | 1.N.009083 | FILM ROLL RAJNI GOLD | KGS | 0.06 |
| 7.A.001607 | RAJNI GOLD REFINED PALMOLEIN OIL BOX | 1.N.009084 | KRAFT CARTON BOX | NOS | 1.00 |
| 7.A.001607 | RAJNI GOLD REFINED PALMOLEIN OIL BOX | 1.N.005814 | BOPP TAPE | NOS | 0.00 |
| 7.A.001329 | RAJNI GOLD REFINED PALMOLEIN OIL | 1.N.009083 | FILM ROLL RAJNI GOLD | KGS | 0.09 |

Important processing rules:

- One SKU may have multiple RM components.
- The same SKU may appear in multiple rows.
- Every row represents one BOM component.
- Blank rows must be ignored.
- Repeated SKU codes must not be treated as duplicate records if their RM codes differ.
- SKU codes and RM codes must be stored as TEXT, preserving dots, letters, leading zeros, and special characters.
- Never convert codes into numbers.
- Do not truncate long descriptions.
- Zero norms are valid and must not automatically be deleted.
- Missing or invalid norms must be flagged for correction.
- Do not silently discard invalid BOM records.
- Validate that each SKU has an identifiable SKU name and each RM has an identifiable material description and UOM.
- The application must support Excel files containing multiple sheets and let the user select the correct sheet if necessary.
- Automatically recognize the six columns even if their positions change.
- If headers are slightly different, provide a column-mapping screen.

### BOM CALCULATION LOGIC

The application must calculate:

Material Requirement = Production Quantity × BOM Norms

However, the meaning of the production quantity and the unit represented by the BOM norms must be confirmed or configured before final calculations.

Provide a configurable production unit setting and, if necessary, a conversion factor for cartons, pouches, bottles, kilograms, or litres.

Never assume that a planned quantity of 10,000 automatically means 10,000 individual units or 10,000 cartons.

If the production quantity unit is unclear, ask the user to configure it before processing the plan.

