# 14. IMPORTANT BUSINESS RULES

These rules are mandatory.

1. The application has exactly three required input files: Combined SKU + BOM Master, Store Stock, and Production Plan.

2. SKU Master and BOM Master must be treated as one combined Excel file.

3. BOM RM codes must match Store Stock Itemcode.

4. SKU codes and material codes must always be treated as text.

5. All material requirements must be calculated from the uploaded BOM norms.

6. Consolidate the same RM code across all planned SKUs, provided UOMs are consistent.

7. Do not combine quantities with different UOMs.

8. Ready Stock For Production is the recommended default available stock figure. WIP must remain separate unless the user explicitly selects another stock policy.

9. Do not double-count stock fields.

10. Do not invent prices or material requirements.

11. Do not silently ignore missing records or calculation errors.

12. Provide complete calculation traceability from production SKU to BOM component to consolidated RM requirement to stock comparison.

13. The procurement recommendation must consider MOQ, reorder level, reorder quantity, existing pending requirements, and procurement lead time when reliable data is available.

14. All reports and dashboard KPIs must use the same calculation engine.

15. If a required business assumption is unknown, ask the user or provide a configurable setting before calculating.

