# 15. SAMPLE VALIDATION TEST

Before declaring the application complete, test the calculation engine using this sample:

Production plan:

| SKU | Planned Quantity |
|---|---:|
| 7.A.001607 | 10,000 |
| 7.A.001329 | 5,000 |

BOM:

| SKU | RM | UOM | Norms |
|---|---|---|---:|
| 7.A.001607 | 1.N.009083 | KGS | 0.06 |
| 7.A.001329 | 1.N.009083 | KGS | 0.09 |

Expected consolidated requirement:

- SKU 7.A.001607: 10,000 × 0.06 = 600 KGS.
- SKU 7.A.001329: 5,000 × 0.09 = 450 KGS.
- Total RM 1.N.009083 requirement = 1,050 KGS.

If Store Stock Ready Stock For Production = 800 KGS:

- Required = 1,050 KGS.
- Available = 800 KGS.
- Shortage = 250 KGS.
- Excess = 0 KGS.

The application must produce these exact results.

Use this as an internal calculation test, not as actual company stock data.

